    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** standing as the clear offensive anchor. With an elite score of 80.65, he benefits from a favorable matchup against a right-handed starter with a 4.31 xERA, while his elite xwOBA of 0.469 and prime spot in the two-hole make him the most reliable producer. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.78) serves as our primary high-upside play; while his platoon splits against a left-handed pitcher usually dampen projections, his lead-off role and the team\u2019s high-weighting on his stolen base potential push him into \"Strong\" start territory. **Lars Nootbaar** also earns a strong recommendation (60.61) as he catches a significant platoon edge against a right-handed arm in a matchup where he should maximize his efficiency in the five-hole.\n\nManaging the bench remains a volatile exercise due to the high volume of \"Lineup Pending\" designations and weather concerns. **Nelson Velazquez** (52.38) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine; despite an elite 0.407 xwOBA, he fell just short of the efficiency threshold when compared to the platoon-advantaged outfielders. We are closely monitoring the rain risk across several venues\u2014notably the 45% risk for **Caleb Durbin** and the 39% risk for both **Pedro Ramirez** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. Should any of these games face significant delays, we are prepared to pivot to **Colt Keith** or **Luke Raley** to ensure we maintain our roster's daily efficiency floor. **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** remain locked in despite facing a challenging arm in Casey Mize, as their ability to provide counting stats\u2014particularly **Trea Turner**'s stolen base upside\u2014remains vital to our 5x5 Roto standing.",
